From u99a06696c483481a at groups.google.com  Tue Aug  1 21:21:58 2017
From: u99a06696c483481a at groups.google.com (Edward Rigdon)
Date: Tue, 01 Aug 2017 21:21:58 +0000
Subject: Re: What should I do if I would like lavaan to return me a matrix with missing values filled by FIML?
Message-ID: <Ijk61cLpvYg.fZkzKH9WAAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <Ijk61cLpvYg.25yHMNELBQAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
References: <Ijk61cLpvYg.25yHMNELBQAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/Ijk61cLpvYg/m/fZkzKH9WAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FIML does not replace missing values. That replacement is called "imputation," and you can use the imputation tools in the semTools package if that is what you want. FIML optimizes an overall likelihood within the context of the missing observations and the free parameters, but it does not supply a set of replacement values for the missing observations.

