> Actzero.model <- 'factor1 =~ NA*BADS3 + c(p3,p3)*BADS3 +

Try removing NA*BADS3 from your syntax.  Instead, use the argument sem(..., std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE) to prevent the first loading from being fixed to 1.  The second group's factor variance will still be estimated because you have specified that in your syntax.

You could also try using the correct number of arguments to the first modifier:  c(NA, NA)*BADS3.  Despite the labels printed in the warning, I imagine the single NA vs. 2 "p3"s is causing the conflict.

