This isn't a lavaan issue, so your question is better posted on SEMNET:

http://www2.gsu.edu/~mkteer/semnet.html

Off the top of my head, if your sample size is small, your chi-squared tests will have low power to detect true effects, while your (delta) AFIs will have increased Type I error rates when using those arbitrary rule-of-thumb cutoffs various people propose in the 2000s.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
