Date: Sun, 20 Aug 2017 21:12:59 +0000
Subject: Odd Suggestion in Modification Indices
Message-ID: <7GqaIZDXIUc.GPMIJyBoCwAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/7GqaIZDXIUc/m/GPMIJyBoCwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear all,

We have been attempting to construct an unconditional autoregressive latent trajectory model with structured residuals (ALT-SR as depicted by Figure 7 in Curran et al., 2014 <https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4067471/>). Below is the code to our model for two variables, “rail” and “dep” observed at four time points. Note that the rail variable intentionally does not include a slope factor because our basic, univariate LGC suggested as much. Further, we have constrained dep’s latent structure to zero because we had several issues with negative and non-positive definite variances and covariances.

modelaltxy <- '
# growth curve rail
# intercept only
i =~ 1*rail1 + 1*rail2 + 1*rail3 + 1*rail4
i ~ 1
i ~~ i

rail1 ~~ rail1
rail2 ~~ rail2
rail3 ~~ rail3
rail4 ~~ rail4

#autoregressive paths for derailment
rail2~a1*rail1
rail3~a2*rail2
rail4~a3*rail3

# growth curve dep
# s2 and i2 variances constrained to zero
i2 =~ 1*dep1 + 1*dep2 + 1*dep3 + 1*dep4
i2 ~ 1
i2 ~~ 0*i2
s2 =~ 0*dep1 + 1*dep2 + 2*dep3 + 3*dep4
s2 ~ 1
s2 ~~ 0*s2
dep1 ~~ dep1
dep2 ~~ dep2
dep3 ~~ dep3
dep4 ~~ dep4

# autoregressive components dep
dep2 ~ b1*dep1
dep3 ~ b2*dep2
dep4 ~ b3*dep3

#cross-sectional covariances
dep1 ~~ rail1
dep2 ~~ rail2
dep3 ~~ rail3
dep4 ~~ rail4

# latent intercept and slope covariances
# except s2s and i2s to zero.
i2~~0*s2
i~~0*s2
i~~0*i2

# crossed effects
dep2 ~ rail1
dep3 ~ rail2
dep4 ~ rail3
rail2 ~ dep1
rail3 ~ dep2
rail4 ~ dep3
'

fit.altxy <- lavaan(modelaltxy, data = ceswide, mimic = "Mplus", missing = "fiml")
summary(fit.altxy,fit.measures=TRUE)
modindices(fit.altxy)

The model does not fit as well as we would like. In attempting to respecify the model, you can see that we called the modification indices. The issue, however, is that one of the most strongly suggested fixes is to specify rail1~1. This is odd to us because we believed that the intercept of rail1 was taken up by the latent intercept of the LGC and, as far as we can tell, the model is correctly specified. As such, we’re left with two questions. First, how is rail1~1 even an option? Second, if we were to free this parameter, what would that even mean?

Thank you for any insights,
Kaylin

