> My question: how do I tell lavaan to estimate latent variables only for one group and not another?

There is an experimental feature that allows you to specify a different model for each group, and the groups can even have different (numbers of) variables in their unique models.

https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/0eS49Cmgrew/bs6J52tJotAJ

Here is an example of how the syntax currently works:

library(lavaan)

HS.model <- '
group: 1
visual  =~ x1 + a*x2 + b*x3
textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6

group: 2
visual  =~ x1 + a*x2 + b*x3
speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9
'

fit <- cfa(HS.model, data=HolzingerSwineford1939, group="school")

